Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS)


*for Ro's Shoe Food, accepting credit card payments means complying with the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard (PCI DSS). PCI DSS is an industry standard designed to protect cardholder data wherever its stored, processed, or transmitted

*even though PCI DSS is only mandatory for organizations that handle payment card data, following it is considered good practice for any business that values data protection.

⦁	purpose: to prevent theft and misuse of payment card information
⦁	version: PCI DSS v4.0 (released March 2022; older versions retired March 2024)
⦁	scope: around 12 main requirements, which expand into roughly 200 detailed controls.
⦁	examples: encryption of cardholder data, restricted storage of account information, and strict access controls


if Ro's team ignores PCI DSS, he risks losing partnerships with payment processors and damaging customer trust. adhering to PCI DSS also helps standardize how data is stored, handled, and transmitted, a foundational step in building a trustworthy business.


-----------



